From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 20:55:41 +0200
Subject: clocksource/drivers/sun4i: Report failed reprogramming to clockevents

sun4i_clkevt_next_event() always returned success.  When an arm does not
take, the clockevents core has no way to know and waits forever for an
interrupt that never comes, instead of retrying with a larger delta.

Check that the reload latched, the timer is enabled and the counter is
non-zero, and return -ETIME otherwise.  Per the A13 manual TMR0_MODE
single mode clears the enable bit on expiry, so this also catches an
event that already elapsed.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/clocksource/timer-sun4i.c | 17 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clocksource/timer-sun4i.c b/drivers/clocksource/timer-sun4i.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/clocksource/timer-sun4i.c
+++ b/drivers/clocksource/timer-sun4i.c
@@ -134,6 +134,21 @@ static int sun4i_clkevt_set_periodic(struct clock_event_device *evt)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static int sun4i_clkevt_check_armed(void __iomem *base, u8 timer)
+{
+	if (sun4i_clkevt_wait_reload(base, timer))
+		return -ETIME;
+
+	/* Single mode clears the enable bit once the interval is reached. */
+	if (!(readl(base + TIMER_CTL_REG(timer)) & TIMER_CTL_ENABLE))
+		return -ETIME;
+
+	if (!readl(base + TIMER_CNTVAL_REG(timer)))
+		return -ETIME;
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static int sun4i_clkevt_next_event(unsigned long evt,
 				   struct clock_event_device *clkevt)
 {
@@ -143,7 +158,7 @@ static int sun4i_clkevt_next_event(unsigned long evt,
 	sun4i_clkevt_time_setup(timer_of_base(to), 0, evt - TIMER_SYNC_TICKS);
 	sun4i_clkevt_time_start(timer_of_base(to), 0, false);
 
-	return 0;
+	return sun4i_clkevt_check_armed(timer_of_base(to), 0);
 }
 
 static void sun4i_timer_clear_interrupt(void __iomem *base)
-- 
